Disable AVIF input optimization to mitigate AIKIDO-2026-553733 (GHSA-2xp9-vwfh-vxw4).

The Next.js Image Optimization API decodes attacker-supplied / remotely-fetched
AVIF images through sharp, which relies on libheif. A crafted AVIF triggers a
heap buffer overflow in libheif during decode/scale, allowing unauthenticated
remote code execution in the Next.js server process.

This backports the upstream fix (vercel/next.js commit 409772ec) to the compiled
JavaScript shipped in the npm tarball (package/dist/**). AVIF input is passed
through untouched instead of being decoded.

